summary:
Leaders at the State University of New York’s 64 campuses have until the end of the year to establish or update artificial intelligence guidelines, including standards for bias evaluation, student data privacy and responsible AI use.
The mandate comes from a binding AI governance policy passed in May, leaving higher ed IT leaders at SUNY campuses to devise ways to evaluate AI vendors, implement governance workflows, protect institutional data and support responsible AI adoption at scale.&nbsp;
